    "common.valuePeriod" : {
      "comment" : "A spoken clause of an announcement ended with a full stop. %@ is the clause. English adds a full stop; change only the mark.\nEnds a line about waiting downloads as a sentence of its own. %@ is the line, such as \"2 waiting for room on this Mac\".\nEnds a line of a progress display with its full stop, so VoiceOver reads the lines as sentences. %@ is the line.\nEnds a sentence with its full stop. %@ is the sentence without it. Chinese and Japanese use their own full stop here.\nEnds a title with a full stop so it reads as a sentence before the question that follows. %@ is the title.\nEnds the notifications setting's hint with a full stop, before the sentence that says notifications are refused. %@ is the hint, without its full stop.\nLibrary view editor: ends a filter's description with a full stop. %@ is the whole description.\nLibrary view editor: the note shown in place of the sort choice while the view lists feeds alone. %@ is a sentence without its full stop, saying feeds are always listed by title; this adds the full stop.\nMakes a clause into a whole sentence by adding its full stop. %@ is the clause, already starting with a capital letter.\nVoiceOver announcement of Next in Folder or Previous in Folder when no item lies that way. %@ is a sentence without its full stop, such as \"No more books in folder\"; this adds the full stop.",
