    "sentence.commaJoined" : {
      "comment" : "A heading's description followed by a detail such as its duration. %1$@ is the description, such as \"Chapter One - level 1\"; %2$@ is the detail, such as \"4 minutes\".\nJoins two parts of a label with a comma. %1$@ is the text so far and %2$@ the next part. English puts a comma and a space between them.\nText of the Library window's View pop-up and Go to View. What a window says on going to the view name by Go to View's key or menu item: the name, then counts, what the view lists there (CountWording.listItems(of:feeds:)), as \"All Items, 743 books, 2 feeds\". Placeholders in order: name, counts.\nThe right side of a row in the Library views settings: whether the view is built in or custom, then when it shows. %1$@ is built in or custom and %2$@ is its visibility, such as \"always\".",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
